          "start_sec": 0.0,
          "end_sec": 44.12,
          "duration_sec": 44.12,
          "transcript_text": "Most people try to build better habits by relying on motivation, and that is the first mistake. Motivation is a feeling, and feelings change from one day to the next. A system, on the other hand, keeps working even when you do not feel like it. Here is a simple example from my own week. I wanted to read more, so I put one book on my desk where I make coffee every morning. That single change removed the decision, and reading became automatic within four days. Why does this work so well? Because you are designing the environment instead of fighting your own willpower. The second tip is to make the first step almost embarrassingly small. Instead of promising to exercise for an hour, promise to put on your shoes.",
